  "note": "ISO 2026-W37 runs from September 7 through September 13. Fixed-sky highlights include Peacock, M29. Venus is about 3.9° in ecliptic longitude from Spica in Virgo. Uranus is about 4.1° in ecliptic longitude from Aldebaran in Taurus.\n\n**Naked eye:** 🌑 New Moon — 03:27:00 UTCα1 Cap — V 4 — Tropical SummerAlgedi (α2 Cap) — V 4 — Tropical Summer. The dark Moon favors faint targets and extended star fields. Use Peacock as the week’s fixed-sky framework.\n\n**Planets:** Venus is about 3.9° in ecliptic longitude from Spica in Virgo. Uranus is about 4.1° in ecliptic longitude from Aldebaran in Taurus.\n\n**Binoculars:** Favor M29, Peacock; wide fields help connect the charted geometry to the real sky.\n\n**Small telescope:** Concentrate on M29. Increase magnification only after the target and surrounding pattern are secure.",
